error_signature: "os.mkfifo.*PermissionError.*EPERM.*HMDFS|mkfifo.*Operation not permitted.*storage"
root_cause: "HMDFS does not support POSIX named pipes (FIFO): os.mkfifo() raises EPERM on /storage HMDFS paths regardless of mode/permissions; upstream tools using mkfifo for inter-process streaming crash at startup."
rec_approach: "Runtime capability probe (PF5-compliant, no platform macro): wrap mkfifo in try/except EPERM->fallback to plain temp files with equivalent data flow (extract fully first, then feed consumer); probe once per run and cache the decision. Reference impl: megahit 1.2.9 patch 0003 wrapper script."
match_keywords: ["mkfifo", "EPERM", "PermissionError", "HMDFS", "named pipe", "FIFO", "fallback"]
error_excerpt: "PermissionError: [Errno 1] Operation not permitted"
severity: P1
category: platform
last_updated: 2026-09-28
